      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-11-11_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <p>TO the Lady who is determined to keep her Dress Expenditure down to the lowest possible minimum consistent with dignity and comfort, our present exposition</p>
        <p>of Autumn Attire will suggest many delightful ways and means. From a smartly Tailored serviceable Costume to the neatest and nattiest of Ready-to-wear Hats everything is provided in the best of taste at obviously moderate prices. We would especially commend to your notice the Homespun and Tweed Costumes, because for once in a way Fashion has declared in favour of the strictly useful, and more practical Suits for daily wear could not be desired. The crowning glory of the Autumn Wardrobe is, of course, the Fur Coat, and the selection placed before you in the 'Dutton Salons rep-</p>
        <p>resents the art of the Furrier at its very best. But every Department is fully and freely open to your inspection, and value—plain, unmistakable value—makes the final and most convincing appeal of all.</p>
