      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-11-11_WidnesExaminer_art0076" n="art0076">
        <head>MONSTER MATINEE</head>
        <p>MONSTER MATINEE</p>
        <p>A'L' I'HE ROYAL COURT THEATRE, WARRINGTON (Kindly lent by the Management), 181.11, at 2.30.</p>
        <p>On SATURDAY NEXT, NOVEMBER • GIGANTIC PROGRAMME:— Members of the Dramatic Society (Mrs. R. Garnett, Mrs. Budd, Mr. S. Wallhead and Mr. H. Moseley) in Sir J. M. Barrie's Comedy, "The Twelve Pound Look." Mr. Harold Raynor, Mr. John Blake and Miss Ennis Lawson in a striking little play, " Love versus Law." Mr. Lewys James and Miss Raymond Amy (members of the Harrison Frewin Opera Company. Miss Olga Hughes' pupils in a little word- less play. Mr. A. W. Pearce. Miss Cook (of the Manchester Concerts). Augmented Theatre Orchestra (under direction of Mr. W. C. Pike). Accompanist, Mr. W. H. Payton, Mus.Bac. Hon. Treasurer, Mr. Arthur Browne. Organisers, Mrs. R. Garnett, Mrs. Fox. Mr. H. L. Warburton, Dress Circle and Stall. 2/2. Upper Circle. 1/8. Si de Circle, 1/2. Pit and Gallery, 7d. Plan opens Monday next.</p>
