      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-11-11_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <head>WARRINGTONIANS IN INDITE</head>
        <p>WARRINGTONIANS IN INDITE</p>
        <p>National Reserve Men Who Volunteered For Service Abroad.</p>
        <p>DO YOU KNOW ANY OF THESE MEN?</p>
        <p>Top Row :--71iflemen B. Bennett, T. Finnerty, J. Hynes, T. McGuire, J. 3fannion, E. Smithson, A. Hargreaves. Mrddle Row :—Riflemen W. Stacey, T. H. Healer, Sergeant J. Hough, Riflemen D. Rowlands, P. Higgins. Bottom Row.—Riflemen W. Powers, W. Thorniley, G. Trantrum.</p>
        <p>We have this week received the above photograph from a number of Warrington National Reserve men serving in the Rifle Brigade in India. Rifleman T. H. Healer, writing for himself and townsmen, says :—" There are friends in Warrington who would like to know where we are serving at present.: We are all National Reserve men who have volunteered to serve His. Majesty abroad."</p>
