      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-11-11_WidnesExaminer_art0110" n="art0110">
        <p>his wife, Mrs. A. Johnson, 16, Marbury-street, Latchford, will be pleased to receive news from his comrades whereby she might be able to discover any trace of him..</p>
        <p>Private Johnson, who enlisted in March of this year, had only been in France eight weeks. He is 33 years of age, a former employe of Messrs. Fletcher. Russell and Co.. Ltd., and was associated with Kent-street- Mission.</p>
        <p>Had A Clear Field. Madge: "Did you have anything to talk about at the -club. meeting?" Marjorie: " Lots. On account of the storm there were only three of us present."</p>
