        <p>INCREASED IMPORTS AND EXPORTS.</p>
        <p>Board of Trade returns for October show that the imports were valued at £81,135,376, an increase of X 13,318,970 on 1915 and X 29,755,941 on 1914, about half of the increase in each case</p>
        <p>being due to cotton and other raw materials. The exports of British produce and manufac- tures were valued at £41,715,248, an' increase of 0212,746,283 on 1915 and 0216,113,433 on 1914. Cotton and woollen goods and coal, Coke, and manufactured fuel showed the biggest in- creases.</p>
      </div>
