        <p>THE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON is prepared to receive LOANS either for six months' notice or for a term of years. Applications, stating amount for investment, to be made to the Borough Treasurer, Municipal Offices, Warrington. EMMANUEL CHURCH, WARRINGTON. THE ANNUAL SALE OF WORK will (D.V.) be held in the CHURCH INSTITUTE, KNUTSFORD-ROAD. ON WEDNESDAY, THURSDAY &amp; FRIDAY. NOVEMBER 15th, 16th. and 17th. The Sale will be opened on Wednesday by THOMAS WILSON, Esq.. of Liscard, at 3 p.m. On Thursday by Mrs. JAMES DODDS, of Penketh, at 3 p.m.. and On Friday by the Rev. FREDERICK L. GROSVENOR, at 7 p.m. MUSICAL ITEMS &amp; OTHER ATTRACTIONS. ADMISSION: First Day. 6d.; Second Day„ 3d.; Third Day, 3d.; Season Ticket, 1/-. TEMPERANCE SUNDAY. A PUBLIC MEETING will be held in the • CO-OPERATIVE HALL, WARRINGTON, TO-MORROW (SUNDAY) EVENING. NOV. 12th. Speakers: Rev. A. LEATHLEY HEAP, B.A. (Leeds), Rev. IRVINE LISTER. Chair to be taken at 8.15 13. M. by Mrs. JAMES DODDS, President of Warrington Band of Hope Union. COLLECTION TO DEFRAY EXPFiNSES. WARRINGTON INSURANCE COMMITTEE. CHANGE OF DOCTOR. ANY INSURED PERSON within the area of the Warrington Insurance Committee, WEW DESIRES TO BE ATTENDED after the 31st December next BY A DOCTOR OTHER THAN THE DOCTOR FROM WHOM HE IS ENTITLED TO OBTAIN TREATMENT during the current year, MUST GIVE NOTICE to the Committee BEFORE THE 12th DECEMBER NEXT. Such notice must be in writing (signed by the insured person), and must be accompanied by the Medical Card. Insured persons on the list of a doctor holding a, Coznmission in the Army or Navy will not be en- titled to change their doctor at the end of the year unless they satisfy the Medical Service Sub-Com- tnittee that they have reasonable grounds for desir- ing to change, in which case they must send to me along with their Medical Card. a full statement of the reasons on which the application to choose another doctor is based. Dated this Bth day of November, 1916. ALFRED TILLING, Clerk to the Committee. Trinity Chambers, Market Gate. Warrington.</p>
