        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in "The Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words. 1/6 each; every additional seven words. 6d.</p>
        <p>Deaths. ALLEN.—On November sth, at 40, Grosfield-street, Charles Allen, in his 73rd year. the dearly beloved husband of Rosannah Allen. Interred at the War- rington Cemetery November Bth: Will friends kindly accept this, the only intimation. SHUTT.—On November 4th, at 267, Lovely-lane, Josiah Shutt. aged 43 years. TOWEY.--On November 7th, at 17, Pierpoint-street, Thomas Towey. aged 59 years. WOOD.—On November sth. at 9, Mill-street, James Wood. aged 61 years. YARWOOD.—At her daughter's residence at Swansea, Mary Yarwood. late of Latchford, in her 90th year. Interred at Hill Cliffe November 9th, 1916. In Memoriam. CHILTON.—In memory of Sapper E. Chilton, our dear brother, who was killed in France November 11th. 1915. Gone is the face we loved so dear, Silent is the voice we loved to hear. ANDREW. ALICE &amp; BABY EDITH. Acknowledgments. AIRS. ALLEN and FAMILY beg to convey their grateful THANKS to all the kind friends for their sympathy in their hour of grief. 40, Crosfield-street, Warrington. MRS. DEELEY and FAMILY desire to THANK their many friends for their kind letters of .sympathy sent to them in their recent sad bereavement. 83, Longford-street, Warrington. MR. and MRS. JOHN LONGSHAW and FAMILY desire to THANK their many friends and relatives for kind letters of sympathy in their sad bereavement. Lynhurst, Thelwall New-road, Grappenhall.</p>
