        <p>PRIVATE GEO. FEARNLEY. . Wounded.</p>
        <p>that "the wound is not very bad, and I have got up from bed." Private Fearnley, who is twenty years of age. was formerly employed by the Pearson and' Knowles Co., Ltd. An "old boy "of the Silier- street School, he enlisted seven months ago, and had been at the Front seven weeks when he received his wound. PRIVATE J. T. HARRISON. • City Marshal Of The R.A.0.8. Ilas Leg Fractured. Private John Thos. Harrison, of the South Lancs. Regiment, was wounded in the leg on October 21st, and has been removed to a London hospital. From there he writes to his parents, Mr. and Mrs. J. T. Harrison, 27, Market-street, as follows :—" I am very glad to be in England once more. We went over the top at twelve o'clock, and took the German trenches, which we had only been in about an hour when I got wounded. At the dressing station they said it was only a slight wound, but when I got • to hospital I had to go under an operation, and</p>
